# Imperial Frontend Architecture

## Overview
The Imperial frontend (shell) is a modern React application built with TypeScript, Vite, and React Router. It provides an AI-powered UI generation interface with real-time streaming updates, authentication, and component library management.

## Core Technologies
- **Framework**: React 19 with TypeScript
- **Build Tool**: Vite with gzip compression
- **Router**: React Router v7
- **State Management**: TanStack Query (React Query) for server state
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with custom design system
- **UI Components**: Radix UI primitives + shadcn/ui
- **Forms**: React Hook Form with Zod validation
- **HTTP Client**: Axios with interceptors
- **Real-time**: Server-Sent Events (SSE) via EventSource
- **Authentication**: JWT with refresh token rotation

